  m_Name: 1992 gum
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: 'Chewing Gum Ban 1992 '
  info: Singapore banned the sale and import of chewing gum to prevent littering
    and damage to public infrastructure, especially MRT train doors. The law was
    enacted after repeated incidents of gum causing costly delays and maintenance
    issues. While chewing gum cannot be sold commercially, medicinal and therapeutic
    gum, such as nicotine gum, is allowed under strict regulations. Offenders may
    face fines of up to SGD 100,000 or imprisonment for large-scale importation,
    while individual violations result in lighter fines.
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4a4ae438d3b4b47c7996954f2fbb7f3c, type: 3}
